gamemaster (0.1.7) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * 'gamemaster add zomboid' without -d looks for the server in the home
    directory of the user as well, and says what to do when it finds
    several or none.
  * Skills for AI agents in /usr/share/doc/gamemaster/skills: switching
    worlds, new worlds, mods, restoring a backup, troubleshooting, and
    background knowledge. SOUL.md is shorter and points to them.
  * The service stops the server with SIGINT, as Ctrl+C does, so it saves
    the world when systemd stops it or the machine shuts down. Units
    written by 0.1.6 get it with 'zomboid service'.

 -- AlfaAlf <git@alfaalf-media.de>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:00:00 +0200

gamemaster (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New command 'zomboid fix-permissions': gives everything below ~/Zomboid
    back to the server user. Server/, Saves/ and mods/ may be changed by the
    agent, db/ belongs to the server alone, the rest may be read. Links are
    never followed, only reported.
  * The service runs fix-permissions before every start and the server with
    UMask=0007. Units written by an older version do not have this yet;
    'zomboid world switch' to the loaded world writes them again.
  * 'gamemaster add' and 'install' put the data directory in order.
  * The agent user gets umask 0007 through pam_umask (GECOS field).
  * Files and directories are created as root without following links;
    the database of a world is no longer open to the agent.
  * The data directory is taken from the home of the server user;
    PZ_SERVER_DATA_DIR is no longer read.
  * The configuration of a server can add ExecStartPre, ExecStartPost and
    ExecStopPost commands to its service (PZ_EXEC_START_PRE_1 and so on).
    A command run as root is only accepted when it and every directory
    above it can be changed by root alone; /etc/gamemaster/hooks is there
    for such scripts.
  * New command 'zomboid service': writes the service again from the
    configuration without stopping the server.
  * First unit tests.

 -- AlfaAlf <git@alfaalf-media.de>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200

gamemaster (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First package. Sets a machine up with 'gamemaster' and runs Project
    Zomboid servers with 'zomboid'.

